body.p:
However, given Mahajan's failure to describe the measurement of a membrane potential of the diaphragm in order to perform EMG thereof, the teachings of Mesin cannot be properly applied to Mahajan's disclosure in a way that results in Applicant's claimed invention since the teachings of Mahajan and Mesin are not compatible in as much as Mahajan's disclosure is directed to detecting thoracic motion and expansion using displacement sensors. See Mahajan, at paragraphs [0016], [0033] and [0070]. In contrast to Mahajan's teachings, Mesin describes detecting EMG signals, but does not describe how such EMG signal detection teachings of Mesin could be incorporated into Mahajan's disclosure to render Applicant's currently clarified invention wherein the wearable device is configured for performing electromyography of~SVG
